chip y8950
clock 3579545
samples 20000
mem adpcm-b y8950.bin
# Recording to external memory: with 0x07 = 0x60 (record, external), each
# data write (0x0f) goes out through the interface (recorded as events)
# and advances, the first one loading the start address; at the end
# address EOS is set and the write is dropped, so the last byte of the
# span keeps its old value. Then the recorded bytes play back. Recording
# again over the sine leaves part of it rewritten. Data writes with start
# and record both set go nowhere, and the channel does not play.
# The image y8950.bin (written by tests/adpcm.rs): 1 KB segments at 0x000
# (a sine), 0x400 (a ramp), 0x800 (noise) and 0xc00 (a square loud enough
# to clamp), then a 4 KB chirp at 0x1000. In RAM with 1-bit access (0x08
# bits 0-1 clear) an address unit is 4 bytes, in ROM or 8-bit RAM 32 bytes.
# Register 0x07 is ADPCM-B's control (0x80 start, 0x40 record, 0x20
# external memory, 0x10 repeat, 0x08 speaker off, 0x01 reset), 0x09-0x0c
# the start and end, 0x0f the data, 0x10-0x11 delta-N, 0x12 the level.
# The status read (offset 0) shows 0x08 BRDY, 0x10 EOS and 0x01 playing.
0 w 0 08 1 00
0 w 0 09 1 00 0 0a 1 04 0 0b 1 0f 0 0c 1 04  # 0x1000-0x103f, 64 bytes over the chirp
0 r 0
10 w 0 07 1 60  # record, external: two dummy reads pending
